  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>-Sulphate - <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>III</mi></math> (Laxative effect)</p><p>Sulfates are a large part of the haze pollution that&nbsp;irritates the lungs and affects your lung health.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>-Fluoride - <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math>&nbsp;(Bending of bones)</p><p>Fluoride is a neurotoxin which,&nbsp;in high doses, can be harmful. Excessive exposure can lead to tooth discoloration and bone problems.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>-Nictoine - <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;(pesticides)</p><p>Nicotine has been used as a <span style=\"background-color:null;\">natural</span><span style=\"background-color:null;\"> </span> insecticide and is the archetype for the large range of synthetic neonicotinoid insecticides.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>-Sodium Arsinite - <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>IV</mi></math>&nbsp;(herbicide)</p><p>Inorganic arsenicals (arsenic trioxide,&nbsp;<em>sodium arsenite</em>&nbsp;and lead arsenate) have been used as rodenticides and herbicides.</p></blockquote>"
